WEBVTT

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.142 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:35.002 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:39.631 line:80%
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:41.008 line:80%
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:42.468 --> 00:00:44.678 line:80%
[Chan] I'm not someone
who will leave in three months,

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:47.389 line:80%
nor someone who might never come back.

00:00:47.473 --> 00:00:49.141 line:80%
Ms. Song, I want to stay

00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:50.267 line:80%
with you.

00:00:51.268 --> 00:00:53.646 line:80%
No, Haran. So I'll tell you everything.

00:00:54.396 --> 00:00:57.816 line:80%
But to tell you everything precisely,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.526 line:80%
I need some time.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.653 line:80%
It won't take long.

00:01:01.236 --> 00:01:03.947 line:80%
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

00:01:04.448 --> 00:01:06.408 line:80%
So when I do,

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:08.452 line:80%
please listen to everything.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.329 line:80%
-[♪ dramatic music playing]
-[breath trembling]

00:01:10.412 --> 00:01:11.914 line:80%
What if you're not okay?

00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:13.540 line:80%
What if something else happens?

00:01:13.624 --> 00:01:16.502 line:80%
I've been okay, I'm okay now,
and I'll keep being okay.

00:01:16.585 --> 00:01:17.586 line:80%
So…

00:01:19.171 --> 00:01:20.172 line:80%
let's go see

00:01:23.092 --> 00:01:25.010 line:80%
the cherry blossoms in spring.

00:01:25.886 --> 00:01:28.472 line:80%
We'll have shaved ice in summer,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.724 line:80%
see the autumn leaves in fall,

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.768 line:80%
and in winter…

00:01:34.603 --> 00:01:36.355 line:80%
it would be fun to go snowboarding.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:40.651 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:01:43.696 --> 00:01:45.489 line:20%
EPISODE 10

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.116 line:20%
[♪ music continues]

00:01:50.285 --> 00:01:52.162 line:20%
[Haran] I think you dropped your bracelet.

00:01:52.246 --> 00:01:53.247 line:20%
[bracelet clinking]

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.498 line:20%
This is yours, right?

00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:00.295 line:20%
Oh. Hey, crybaby Song Haran.

00:02:00.796 --> 00:02:01.839 line:20%
[chuckles]

00:02:05.134 --> 00:02:06.969 line:20%
[♪ music swells]

00:02:10.055 --> 00:02:11.974 line:20%
[♪ music continues]

00:02:20.024 --> 00:02:22.568 line:80%
-Let's go.
-Let me return her bracelet.

00:02:23.235 --> 00:02:25.779 line:80%
[metallic clinking, clattering]

00:02:25.863 --> 00:02:28.824 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[exclaims] Oh, no. I'm sorry. Oh…

00:02:30.075 --> 00:02:32.494 line:80%
-Get your stuff. I'll do this.
-[stutters]

00:02:34.788 --> 00:02:36.123 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I came to ask you for help.</i>

00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:38.042 line:80%
<i>I really want to protect something,</i>

00:02:38.125 --> 00:02:40.502 line:80%
but to do that, I need my memories.

00:02:40.586 --> 00:02:41.587 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.672 line:80%
It's okay. It breaks sometimes.

00:02:43.756 --> 00:02:46.216 line:80%
I've been wearing it for a long time.

00:02:48.427 --> 00:02:49.511 line:80%
[Chan] I'm sorry.

00:02:50.888 --> 00:02:53.349 line:80%
I'm sorry, I'll get it repaired for you.

00:02:53.432 --> 00:02:56.101 line:80%
It's really fine, Haran.

00:02:58.604 --> 00:02:59.605 line:80%
Excuse me?

00:02:59.688 --> 00:03:01.899 line:80%
Ah. Your name was written on the pen.

00:03:03.025 --> 00:03:04.276 line:80%
That's a pretty name.

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:08.906 line:80%
-Let's go.
-He seems to be in quite a hurry.

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:10.366 line:80%
You can go. It's fine.

00:03:12.368 --> 00:03:13.911 line:80%
[hesitates] I'm really sorry…

00:03:15.788 --> 00:03:17.081 line:80%
Why are you so on edge?

00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:22.461 line:80%
[stutters] No, wait. I'm sorry.
You should hurry home and get some rest.

00:03:22.544 --> 00:03:24.254 line:80%
Did the doctor say you're okay?

00:03:24.922 --> 00:03:25.923 line:80%
Yes, I'm fine.

00:03:26.423 --> 00:03:27.466 line:80%
So let's go.

00:03:38.727 --> 00:03:40.729 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:03:42.272 --> 00:03:45.359 line:80%
If you feel dizzy or uncomfortable,
tell me straightaway.

00:03:50.447 --> 00:03:51.448 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:54.368 line:80%
Sir.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.246 line:80%
I'm sorry, but can you pull over nearby?

00:03:58.414 --> 00:04:00.082 line:80%
Shouldn't you get some rest?

00:04:00.582 --> 00:04:01.667 line:80%
I'm totally fine.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.963 line:80%
Oh? There's a look of doubt on your face.

00:04:06.922 --> 00:04:10.092 line:80%
[sighs heavily] Then I'll do 100 push-ups!

00:04:10.175 --> 00:04:11.176 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.137 line:80%
All right, fine. I believe you.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.099 line:80%
I feel like we'll just feel down
and regret it if we go home now.

00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:18.600 line:80%
So…

00:04:18.684 --> 00:04:20.394 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:04:20.477 --> 00:04:24.231 line:80%
let's begin Seonu Chan's
birthday gift ceremony.

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.944 line:80%
That's my present, right?

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.155 line:80%
This…

00:04:31.238 --> 00:04:32.489 line:80%
[Chan] Oh… Let me guess.

00:04:33.073 --> 00:04:35.868 line:80%
Mmm… It's clothes.

00:04:36.577 --> 00:04:39.997 line:80%
A cardigan you designed yourself.

00:04:40.622 --> 00:04:42.291 line:80%
How did you know?

00:04:42.374 --> 00:04:43.751 line:80%
I prepared this in secret.

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:45.627 line:80%
It was obvious.

00:04:45.711 --> 00:04:46.837 line:80%
It was?

00:04:47.963 --> 00:04:50.007 line:80%
Oh. I see…

00:04:51.383 --> 00:04:54.136 line:80%
-Hang on. Just give me five minutes.
-[stutters]

00:04:56.013 --> 00:04:59.600 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you </i>♪

00:04:59.683 --> 00:05:02.269 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you </i>♪

00:05:02.353 --> 00:05:05.731 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy birthday, dear Seonu Chan </i>♪

00:05:05.814 --> 00:05:07.900 line:80%
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you </i>♪

00:05:07.983 --> 00:05:09.318 line:80%
[cheers]

00:05:09.401 --> 00:05:10.778 line:80%
[exclaims] Wait.

00:05:10.861 --> 00:05:12.696 line:80%
You should still make a wish

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:15.616 line:80%
even if it's just a humble
convenience store cake.

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:17.368 line:80%
Then make a wish with me.

00:05:27.127 --> 00:05:28.170 line:80%
[inhales]

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.799 line:80%
Wow! [laughs]

00:05:31.882 --> 00:05:33.133 line:80%
What did you wish for?

00:05:33.717 --> 00:05:36.470 line:80%
It's a secret.
If I share it, it won't come true.

00:05:36.553 --> 00:05:38.013 line:80%
Right.

00:05:38.097 --> 00:05:39.890 line:80%
-[Chan clears throat]
-Then…

00:05:39.974 --> 00:05:42.643 line:80%
I'll give you your birthday present now.

00:05:42.726 --> 00:05:45.062 line:80%
-Happy birthday.
-Oh. Can I open it right now?

00:05:46.772 --> 00:05:48.315 line:80%
[♪ pleasant song playing]

00:05:49.274 --> 00:05:50.567 line:80%
[Chan exclaims excitedly]

00:05:52.987 --> 00:05:54.238 line:80%
Huh?

00:05:54.321 --> 00:05:57.199 line:80%
I didn't know about this.

00:05:57.282 --> 00:05:59.326 line:80%
[exclaims] At least
I kept one thing a secret.

00:06:00.369 --> 00:06:01.412 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:06:01.912 --> 00:06:03.163 line:80%
I'm glad I was born.

00:06:04.915 --> 00:06:07.126 line:80%
Song Haran wished me happy birthday.

00:06:08.836 --> 00:06:11.880 line:80%
[inhales sharply, yells] Everybody!
Song Haran wished me happy birthday!

00:06:12.798 --> 00:06:14.591 line:80%
[stutters] Are you crazy?

00:06:14.675 --> 00:06:15.843 line:80%
-[Haran chuckles softly]
-[Chan inhales sharply]

00:06:15.926 --> 00:06:19.638 line:80%
I'll wear this every day,
in spring, summer, fall, and winter.

00:06:19.722 --> 00:06:21.724 line:80%
I'll wear this to bed, too.

00:06:21.807 --> 00:06:25.519 line:80%
-Ah. And even when I'm showering.
-[Haran chuckles]

00:06:26.395 --> 00:06:29.773 line:80%
I wanted to do more for you
since it's our first birthday together.

00:06:33.152 --> 00:06:34.695 line:80%
Since you seem upset,

00:06:35.404 --> 00:06:36.405 line:80%
how about a date tomorrow?

00:06:36.488 --> 00:06:39.408 line:80%
We can watch a movie,
have a nice meal, hold hands,

00:06:39.491 --> 00:06:41.744 line:80%
and take a walk while we chat.

00:06:41.827 --> 00:06:43.495 line:80%
We'll do what other couples do.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.166 line:80%
You should just rest. I'm worried.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:51.295 line:80%
[sighs dejectedly] You leave me
no choice, then. I should do push-ups…

00:06:51.378 --> 00:06:54.298 line:80%
-[exclaims] All right. Let's go on a date.
-[clears throat]

00:06:54.381 --> 00:06:55.632 line:80%
[scoffs]

00:06:55.716 --> 00:07:00.471 line:80%
But can you sing that part again?

00:07:01.347 --> 00:07:02.598 line:80%
The…

00:07:02.681 --> 00:07:05.559 line:80%
"dear Seonu Chan" part.

00:07:08.187 --> 00:07:10.731 line:80%
I'll make your birthday
even more special next year.

00:07:10.814 --> 00:07:14.068 line:80%
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

00:07:17.946 --> 00:07:19.156 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:07:19.239 --> 00:07:20.240 line:80%
So…

00:07:21.742 --> 00:07:23.494 line:80%
stay healthy, okay?

00:07:31.669 --> 00:07:33.128 line:80%
I will.

00:07:34.254 --> 00:07:35.381 line:80%
Besides,

00:07:35.964 --> 00:07:38.884 line:80%
my mind's filled with you, Haran,

00:07:40.177 --> 00:07:42.846 line:80%
so a tiny fragment in my brain…

00:07:43.764 --> 00:07:45.808 line:80%
[exclaims boastfully] won't affect me.

00:07:56.151 --> 00:07:58.404 line:80%
[♪ song continues]

00:08:00.739 --> 00:08:01.907 line:80%
Sir?

00:08:01.991 --> 00:08:03.283 line:80%
Just a moment.

00:08:15.212 --> 00:08:17.214 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

00:08:17.297 --> 00:08:18.632 line:80%
What?

00:08:19.341 --> 00:08:20.426 line:80%
Why are we…

00:08:22.469 --> 00:08:24.638 line:80%
We were in Chuncheon earlier…

00:08:29.351 --> 00:08:30.561 line:80%
Manjae.

00:08:32.021 --> 00:08:34.398 line:80%
We're here. Let's get off.

00:08:43.115 --> 00:08:44.366 line:80%
[breath trembling]

00:08:46.368 --> 00:08:47.619 line:80%
[Manjae] How long has it been?

00:08:48.245 --> 00:08:49.496 line:80%
Where were you planning

00:08:50.956 --> 00:08:52.624 line:80%
to disappear off to alone?

00:08:53.542 --> 00:08:54.626 line:80%
[Nana] Manjae.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:57.504 line:80%
What do I do?

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.631 line:80%
[♪ emotional music playing]

00:08:59.715 --> 00:09:01.050 line:80%
What do I do about the kids?

00:09:05.554 --> 00:09:06.555 line:80%
I want

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.933 line:80%
to stay with them longer.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.564 line:80%
I want to stay with you longer, too.

00:09:17.483 --> 00:09:19.360 line:80%
But what if I forget everything?

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:24.073 line:80%
[voice shaking] If I end up
forgetting you and the kids…

00:09:27.159 --> 00:09:28.369 line:80%
[sobs]

00:09:28.452 --> 00:09:30.746 line:80%
and everything else…

00:09:34.041 --> 00:09:35.167 line:80%
I'm scared. [sniffles]

00:09:35.959 --> 00:09:37.503 line:80%
[sobbing] I'm terrified.

00:09:39.588 --> 00:09:41.340 line:80%
[Nana continues sobbing]

00:09:43.509 --> 00:09:44.510 line:80%
[Manjae] It's all right.

00:09:45.135 --> 00:09:46.553 line:80%
Everything will be okay.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.849 line:80%
You can let it all out with me.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:53.811 line:80%
Don't worry.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:55.646 line:80%
I will never

00:09:56.522 --> 00:09:57.773 line:80%
let you be alone.

00:09:59.608 --> 00:10:00.776 line:80%
Never.

00:10:00.859 --> 00:10:03.028 line:80%
[Nana crying]

00:10:10.536 --> 00:10:12.538 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:10:19.253 --> 00:10:21.797 line:80%
[inhales sharply] There's one missing.

00:10:28.554 --> 00:10:29.555 line:80%
Huh?

00:10:29.638 --> 00:10:31.849 line:80%
[metallic clinking, clattering]

00:10:33.267 --> 00:10:36.061 line:80%
[sighs wearily] I took one of her charms.

00:10:36.645 --> 00:10:38.022 line:80%
How do I get this back to her?

00:10:42.359 --> 00:10:44.945 line:80%
[doctor] <i>The shrapnel's still lodged deep</i>
<i>in the temporal bone.</i>

00:10:46.238 --> 00:10:47.906 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.367 line:80%
[♪ melancholic music playing]

00:10:57.708 --> 00:10:58.917 line:80%
It's really fine,

00:10:59.501 --> 00:11:00.502 line:80%
Haran.

00:11:10.346 --> 00:11:11.555 line:80%
[Haran] <i>What did you wish for?</i>

00:11:12.514 --> 00:11:14.975 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I won't wish for anything else</i>
<i>for the rest of my life.</i>

00:11:15.893 --> 00:11:18.103 line:80%
<i>Please just let me stay with this person</i>

00:11:18.187 --> 00:11:20.606 line:80%
<i>who let me live again,</i>

00:11:20.689 --> 00:11:24.151 line:80%
<i>through every tear and every smile.</i>

00:11:24.693 --> 00:11:27.446 line:80%
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

00:11:27.988 --> 00:11:29.865 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Just allow me this one thing.</i>

00:11:30.783 --> 00:11:32.868 line:80%
<i>Let me keep staying by her side.</i>

00:11:46.465 --> 00:11:47.758 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:11:53.013 --> 00:11:58.477 line:80%
<i>My birthday, the day I decided</i>
<i>to explain everything,</i>

00:11:59.228 --> 00:12:00.646 line:80%
<i>despite the gaps.</i>

00:12:02.982 --> 00:12:04.984 line:80%
[♪ music swells]

00:12:17.663 --> 00:12:19.581 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.292 line:20%
[♪ music fades]

00:12:22.376 --> 00:12:23.460 line:80%
[Haran sighs]

00:12:23.544 --> 00:12:25.337 line:80%
PETROUS PART OF THE TEMPORAL BONE

00:12:27.131 --> 00:12:29.717 line:80%
-[knock on door]
-[Hayeong] Your sister's coming in.

00:12:31.218 --> 00:12:32.469 line:80%
What?

00:12:32.553 --> 00:12:34.722 line:80%
Are you applying for medical school, too?

00:12:34.805 --> 00:12:36.140 line:80%
I was just looking up something.

00:12:36.223 --> 00:12:37.308 line:80%
Is Grandma still sleeping?

00:12:37.391 --> 00:12:41.270 line:80%
Yeah, it's the first time.
She never slept in, even on the weekends.

00:12:41.353 --> 00:12:44.106 line:80%
[sighs] Is she tired
after her trip to Chuncheon?

00:12:44.732 --> 00:12:46.066 line:80%
But what are those books for?

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:49.361 line:80%
I just thought I'd work
to get my mind off things.

00:12:49.445 --> 00:12:52.990 line:80%
[gasps] Do you have the pigment book?
It wasn't in Grandma's study.

00:12:53.073 --> 00:12:55.826 line:80%
It's probably in the attic. Hmm…

00:12:56.827 --> 00:12:58.662 line:80%
Why are your eyes puffy? Did you cry?

00:12:59.538 --> 00:13:00.998 line:80%
Huh? [chuckles]

00:13:01.081 --> 00:13:03.542 line:80%
[stutters] Of course not.
I just slept well.

00:13:03.625 --> 00:13:05.627 line:80%
Just go and find that book for me.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:09.006 line:80%
[in English] Thank you.

00:13:20.142 --> 00:13:21.769 line:80%
[Chan in Korean] <i>You can overcome it.</i>

00:13:22.853 --> 00:13:24.938 line:80%
<i>You'll be able to escape on your own.</i>

00:13:25.731 --> 00:13:27.149 line:80%
<i>I wanted to show you, too.</i>

00:13:27.232 --> 00:13:29.234 line:80%
[♪ light-hearted music playing]

00:13:36.283 --> 00:13:39.328 line:80%
What are you doing?
Why did you pull up your sleeves?

00:13:39.411 --> 00:13:41.330 line:80%
I want to clear out some stuff.

00:13:41.413 --> 00:13:42.706 line:80%
Like a spring deep clean.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:46.293 line:80%
Get your head together.
It's the middle of winter.

00:13:47.336 --> 00:13:50.172 line:80%
No, it's spring. [chuckles softly]

00:13:56.011 --> 00:13:58.555 line:80%
I don't think I'll wear this.

00:14:00.641 --> 00:14:01.850 line:80%
And this…

00:14:14.071 --> 00:14:15.948 line:80%
-I'm heading out.
-Wait.

00:14:16.532 --> 00:14:18.325 line:80%
-[in English] You've got mail.
-Oh?

00:14:18.409 --> 00:14:21.286 line:80%
[in Korean] He must have sent a letter
since it's so hard to reach you.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:23.914 line:80%
That poor Kang Hyeokchan.

00:14:23.998 --> 00:14:25.499 line:80%
-See you later.
-Huh?

00:14:25.582 --> 00:14:27.668 line:80%
-[cellphone vibrating]
-You're right. Oh…

00:14:29.128 --> 00:14:30.129 line:80%
Yes?

00:14:30.671 --> 00:14:32.339 line:80%
I'll be there right away.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:34.341 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:14:40.472 --> 00:14:42.474 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:46.061 line:20%
[Hyeokchan] <i>Haran, you must still be busy.</i>

00:14:46.145 --> 00:14:49.440 line:80%
<i>It's already been a month</i>
<i>since I came to Boston.</i>

00:14:49.523 --> 00:14:51.692 line:80%
<i>Everything still feels unfamiliar to me.</i>

00:14:51.775 --> 00:14:55.446 line:80%
<i>I miss you, but it's hard to hear</i>
<i>your voice because of the time difference.</i>

00:14:55.529 --> 00:14:57.698 line:80%
<i>I've been thinking</i>
<i>about a way to communicate.</i>

00:14:57.781 --> 00:14:59.616 line:80%
<i>Can you use a messenger at work?</i>

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:00.743 line:80%
<i>Tell me if you can.</i>

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.745 line:80%
<i>Ah. Let me tell you something cool.</i>

00:15:03.329 --> 00:15:05.539 line:80%
<i>My dorm roommate is Korean,</i>

00:15:05.622 --> 00:15:07.082 line:80%
<i>and his name's Chan, too.</i>

00:15:07.166 --> 00:15:08.334 line:80%
[chuckles] <i>Isn't that funny?</i>

00:15:09.001 --> 00:15:11.378 line:80%
<i>But I think it'll be hard</i>
<i>to get close to him.</i>

00:15:11.462 --> 00:15:13.547 line:80%
<i>He seems a bit closed off.</i>

00:15:14.131 --> 00:15:15.883 line:80%
<i>I miss you so much, Haran.</i>

00:15:15.966 --> 00:15:18.052 line:80%
<i>I'll come see you during summer break.</i>

00:15:18.135 --> 00:15:20.220 line:80%
<i>Take care. I love you.</i>

00:15:20.763 --> 00:15:21.764 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:23.641 line:80%
[cellphone vibrates]

00:15:25.601 --> 00:15:28.228 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I booked the movie tickets.</i>
<i>I'll see you at 5:00 p.m.</i>

00:15:28.312 --> 00:15:30.272 line:80%
Oh. I should get ready.

00:15:41.116 --> 00:15:43.118 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[Manjae exclaims]

00:15:44.453 --> 00:15:45.579 line:80%
[Chan] Mr. Park.

00:15:45.663 --> 00:15:48.582 line:80%
I might come home pretty late tonight.

00:15:51.418 --> 00:15:53.212 line:80%
All right.

00:15:53.295 --> 00:15:56.048 line:80%
Talk it out with Haran.

00:15:56.131 --> 00:16:00.135 line:80%
If you're sincere,
I'm sure she'll understand.

00:16:04.932 --> 00:16:06.976 line:80%
-All right. I will.
-Okay.

00:16:16.527 --> 00:16:18.612 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:16:19.822 --> 00:16:21.365 line:80%
They must be in the corner.

00:16:21.448 --> 00:16:24.618 line:80%
[groans] This is broken.
It won't charge. [tuts]

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.582 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

00:16:32.501 --> 00:16:34.920 line:80%
[hesitates] Do you have time
after the movie?

00:16:36.255 --> 00:16:38.173 line:80%
There's something I have to tell you.

00:16:39.174 --> 00:16:42.428 line:80%
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

00:16:44.388 --> 00:16:45.597 line:80%
All right.

00:16:47.349 --> 00:16:49.727 line:80%
Oh? I forgot the other popcorn.

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:51.437 line:80%
I'll go get it.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:53.856 line:80%
-Just wait here.
-I'll wait inside, then.

00:16:55.065 --> 00:16:56.358 line:80%
[crackles]

00:16:57.735 --> 00:16:59.945 line:80%
-[♪ tense music playing]
-[fire crackling]

00:17:02.156 --> 00:17:04.825 line:80%
[breathes deeply]

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:08.412 line:80%
-[staff 1] Sorry about that.
-It's okay.

00:17:08.912 --> 00:17:09.913 line:80%
Thank you.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.792 line:80%
[fire alarm blaring]

00:17:13.876 --> 00:17:15.836 line:80%
-Is it a false alarm?
-What do we do?

00:17:15.919 --> 00:17:18.505 line:80%
[staff 2] Please follow the instructions
and evacuate immediately.

00:17:19.131 --> 00:17:20.132 line:80%
Please don't push.

00:17:20.215 --> 00:17:21.258 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Song Haran.</i>

00:17:22.593 --> 00:17:23.719 line:80%
Please go downstairs.

00:17:24.553 --> 00:17:26.055 line:80%
Don't push!

00:17:26.138 --> 00:17:27.431 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:17:30.768 --> 00:17:32.478 line:80%
[staff 3] Evacuate immediately.

00:17:34.229 --> 00:17:35.856 line:80%
You shouldn't go inside.

00:17:35.939 --> 00:17:36.940 line:80%
Sorry!

00:17:37.024 --> 00:17:38.150 line:80%
-Sir!
-Song Haran!

00:17:39.401 --> 00:17:40.611 line:80%
-Song Haran!
-[loud thud]

00:17:40.694 --> 00:17:42.321 line:80%
[high-pitched ringing]

00:17:45.991 --> 00:17:47.201 line:80%
[loud thud]

00:17:48.035 --> 00:17:49.286 line:80%
[groans, winces]

00:17:50.454 --> 00:17:51.914 line:80%
Stop it!

00:17:52.748 --> 00:17:54.041 line:80%
[groans]

00:17:55.876 --> 00:17:56.919 line:80%
[groans]

00:17:58.045 --> 00:18:00.047 line:80%
[high-pitched ringing]

00:18:01.048 --> 00:18:02.049 line:80%
[grunts]

00:18:04.593 --> 00:18:05.803 line:80%
[Haran] Seonu Chan!

00:18:08.347 --> 00:18:10.307 line:80%
Seonu Chan! [exhales]

00:18:10.808 --> 00:18:11.809 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I'll tell you everything.</i>

00:18:11.892 --> 00:18:15.062 line:80%
<i>I'll tell you about the scars on my body.</i>

00:18:15.145 --> 00:18:17.356 line:80%
<i>I don't do well in noisy places.</i>

00:18:19.024 --> 00:18:21.110 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Seonu Chan! Where are you?</i>

00:18:23.821 --> 00:18:25.572 line:80%
[coughs, exclaims]

00:18:26.073 --> 00:18:27.825 line:80%
-[Chan grunts]
-[gasps softly]

00:18:27.908 --> 00:18:30.077 line:80%
[exclaims worriedly] Where were you?

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.453 line:80%
I couldn't see you outside,

00:18:31.537 --> 00:18:33.455 line:80%
-so I thought you'd gone inside…
-I'm okay.

00:18:34.123 --> 00:18:36.875 line:80%
[pants] I'm so relieved nothing happened.

00:18:37.459 --> 00:18:38.460 line:80%
[Haran exclaims]

00:18:39.044 --> 00:18:40.254 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:18:41.422 --> 00:18:42.631 line:80%
It's okay.

00:18:43.382 --> 00:18:44.967 line:80%
Let's go to the hospital
and get you checked.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:47.136 line:80%
[Chan] I'll get a checkup soon.

00:18:47.636 --> 00:18:49.263 line:80%
[breathing heavily] Don't worry.

00:18:50.472 --> 00:18:52.349 line:80%
I'll be completely fine.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.312 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:19:00.774 --> 00:19:02.026 line:80%
[sighs]

00:19:02.109 --> 00:19:04.028 line:80%
MEDICAL CHECKUP

00:19:04.111 --> 00:19:05.321 line:80%
[door opens, closes]

00:19:07.448 --> 00:19:08.699 line:80%
Grandma.

00:19:08.782 --> 00:19:10.909 line:80%
What is it, Haran? Is something wrong?

00:19:15.956 --> 00:19:16.999 line:80%
What do I do, Grandma?

00:19:17.082 --> 00:19:18.292 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:19:18.375 --> 00:19:20.502 line:80%
He's not well.

00:19:21.712 --> 00:19:23.589 line:80%
He keeps collapsing,

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:26.675 line:80%
and there's something lodged in his head.

00:19:27.468 --> 00:19:29.970 line:80%
He says he's okay,
but he doesn't seem okay at all.

00:19:31.096 --> 00:19:33.724 line:80%
[sighs] What do I do
if something happens to him?

00:19:34.975 --> 00:19:36.852 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I may not be</i>

00:19:36.935 --> 00:19:40.689 line:80%
as good for her as you believe.

00:19:47.613 --> 00:19:49.281 line:80%
He's not keeping it from you.

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:51.158 line:80%
He probably can't

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:52.951 line:80%
because he's scared.

00:19:53.619 --> 00:19:56.205 line:80%
He probably doesn't want
to burden you with his pain

00:19:56.872 --> 00:19:58.248 line:80%
because it would hurt you.

00:19:58.332 --> 00:19:59.458 line:80%
He cares more

00:20:00.292 --> 00:20:02.670 line:80%
about protecting you than his own pain.

00:20:02.753 --> 00:20:04.797 line:80%
But I want to protect him.

00:20:05.964 --> 00:20:08.133 line:80%
I don't want him to go through it alone.

00:20:09.385 --> 00:20:11.762 line:80%
But there's nothing I can do for him.

00:20:11.845 --> 00:20:13.555 line:80%
Just stay by his side.

00:20:14.264 --> 00:20:18.185 line:80%
People can stay strong
even with just one person by their side.

00:20:18.727 --> 00:20:19.770 line:80%
Trust me, I know.

00:20:20.896 --> 00:20:23.482 line:80%
So don't worry too much.

00:20:23.565 --> 00:20:26.443 line:80%
I'm sure you'll find a way.

00:20:33.575 --> 00:20:34.576 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:35.828 line:80%
[Chan sighs]

00:20:43.085 --> 00:20:44.086 line:80%
Waste container…

00:20:44.712 --> 00:20:45.879 line:80%
Kang Hyeokchan…

00:20:46.463 --> 00:20:47.506 line:80%
Lab…

00:20:48.257 --> 00:20:49.425 line:80%
Cha Sujin…

00:20:49.508 --> 00:20:50.968 line:80%
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]
-[loud thud]

00:20:51.051 --> 00:20:52.094 line:80%
[groans, winces]

00:20:52.177 --> 00:20:53.303 line:80%
Stop it!

00:20:53.971 --> 00:20:55.139 line:80%
And me…

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:58.392 line:80%
Was that day…

00:21:00.811 --> 00:21:01.979 line:80%
[explosion]

00:21:02.563 --> 00:21:05.316 line:80%
[Chan]
"Volatile reagent container fractured…"

00:21:05.399 --> 00:21:07.026 line:80%
"Self-reactive event

00:21:07.109 --> 00:21:09.903 line:80%
triggered by careless handling
of reagents."

00:21:10.404 --> 00:21:13.866 line:20%
"The cause has not been
conclusively determined."

00:21:13.949 --> 00:21:14.950 line:80%
No, there's nothing.

00:21:15.034 --> 00:21:16.577 line:80%
I said I don't know!

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.370 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:21:18.454 --> 00:21:22.249 line:80%
What is she trying to hide?

00:21:24.626 --> 00:21:25.753 line:80%
[cellphone vibrates]

00:21:30.049 --> 00:21:31.884 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Don't do anything tomorrow</i>

00:21:31.967 --> 00:21:33.802 line:80%
<i>and get plenty of rest.</i>

00:21:33.886 --> 00:21:35.679 line:80%
<i>I'll always be by your side.</i>

00:21:43.479 --> 00:21:47.107 line:80%
MY BIRTHDAY, THE DAY I DECIDED
TO EXPLAIN EVERYTHING, DESPITE THE GAPS

00:21:50.069 --> 00:21:52.613 line:80%
NEXT TO THE CONTAINER: KANG HYEOKCHAN
IN THE LAB: CHA SUJIN

00:21:55.991 --> 00:21:58.452 line:80%
[groans, inhales deeply]

00:21:58.535 --> 00:22:00.537 line:80%
[exhales heavily]

00:22:03.457 --> 00:22:04.458 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:22:04.541 --> 00:22:06.543 line:80%
12-WEEK REHABILITATION PLAN

00:22:07.086 --> 00:22:09.296 line:80%
Ah. It's tomorrow.

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:14.093 line:80%
But, Mr. Park, when should we tell
Hadam and her sisters?

00:22:14.176 --> 00:22:15.594 line:80%
Yougyum!

00:22:15.678 --> 00:22:17.054 line:80%
Hey, Dad!

00:22:17.137 --> 00:22:18.222 line:80%
Really? Okay.

00:22:18.305 --> 00:22:19.765 line:80%
Is it your dad?

00:22:19.848 --> 00:22:21.517 line:80%
-Let me say hi.
-Okay, Dad.

00:22:22.142 --> 00:22:24.645 line:80%
-[line disconnects]
-I said I wanted to say hi.

00:22:25.688 --> 00:22:27.398 line:80%
Oh, I didn't hear you.

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:30.234 line:80%
-Sorry.
-Gosh.

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:33.612 line:80%
Ta-da. It's pumpkin porridge.

00:22:33.696 --> 00:22:37.574 line:80%
It's rich in beta-carotene and vitamin A,
so it'll help with the inflammation.

00:22:38.158 --> 00:22:39.493 line:80%
Make sure to eat everything.

00:22:48.419 --> 00:22:50.295 line:80%
-Hadam.
-Yes?

00:22:50.879 --> 00:22:53.048 line:80%
You know I like you so, so much, right?

00:22:53.132 --> 00:22:55.259 line:80%
You helped me stay strong
when I was in pain.

00:22:56.010 --> 00:22:58.345 line:80%
If you ever have a hard time someday,

00:22:58.429 --> 00:23:01.932 line:80%
I'll do the same for you
so that you stay strong.

00:23:02.016 --> 00:23:04.059 line:80%
[chuckles softly] Sure.

00:23:04.143 --> 00:23:06.770 line:80%
But that's not going to happen.

00:23:06.854 --> 00:23:09.398 line:80%
Once you're better,
I'll have nothing but happy days ahead.

00:23:09.481 --> 00:23:10.816 line:80%
[both chuckle softly]

00:23:21.076 --> 00:23:22.578 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:23:22.661 --> 00:23:23.829 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:23:29.168 --> 00:23:30.336 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:23:32.379 --> 00:23:33.464 line:80%
Hi.

00:23:33.547 --> 00:23:36.008 line:80%
-Did you have a good weekend?
-Yes.

00:23:36.091 --> 00:23:38.010 line:80%
I'm on my way to meet Mr. Chae.

00:23:38.093 --> 00:23:41.013 line:80%
He sent me files on the material,
but they kept getting corrupted,

00:23:41.096 --> 00:23:42.473 line:80%
so he's bringing them in person.

00:23:42.556 --> 00:23:44.308 line:80%
He must have something to cover nearby.

00:23:45.392 --> 00:23:47.227 line:80%
That's quite a coincidence.

00:23:47.311 --> 00:23:48.437 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:53.776 line:80%
Ah. I was checking the sample dye
from the color team.

00:23:53.859 --> 00:23:55.319 line:80%
I guess it wasn't dry yet.

00:23:56.362 --> 00:23:58.030 line:80%
I'll get going, then.

00:24:00.324 --> 00:24:03.369 line:80%
[sighs] I felt so awkward
I ended up rambling.

00:24:12.753 --> 00:24:14.755 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:24:14.838 --> 00:24:17.549 line:80%
Um… These are the colors
that Ms. Kim directed.

00:24:17.633 --> 00:24:20.302 line:80%
[inhales sharply]
Then this would be the most similar,

00:24:20.386 --> 00:24:23.055 line:80%
but it might look muted on the fabric.

00:24:23.138 --> 00:24:24.181 line:80%
[Seunggyu] I think so, too.

00:24:24.264 --> 00:24:26.183 line:80%
We should try mixing the colors again.

00:24:26.266 --> 00:24:29.144 line:80%
Then let's apply the feedback
and submit a report for now.

00:24:29.228 --> 00:24:31.230 line:80%
-[Raemee] Okay.
-[Pureum sniffs]

00:24:31.313 --> 00:24:32.439 line:80%
Coffee?

00:24:32.523 --> 00:24:34.149 line:80%
All right, everyone.

00:24:34.233 --> 00:24:36.110 line:80%
Fresh coffee.

00:24:36.193 --> 00:24:37.987 line:80%
-Mr. Park.
-Hello.

00:24:38.070 --> 00:24:39.238 line:80%
What brings you here?

00:24:39.321 --> 00:24:41.198 line:80%
I got a new batch of beans.

00:24:41.281 --> 00:24:42.449 line:80%
Gosh.

00:24:42.533 --> 00:24:46.662 line:80%
So I thought I'd deliver some
to my regular customers.

00:24:47.329 --> 00:24:48.998 line:80%
[Sol and Raemee exclaim] Thank you.

00:24:49.081 --> 00:24:51.333 line:80%
-[Manjae] No problem.
-I'm taking this one.

00:24:51.417 --> 00:24:53.043 line:80%
It's totally my style.

00:24:53.127 --> 00:24:54.670 line:80%
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:24:54.753 --> 00:24:57.965 line:80%
-This is reserved for someone else.
-[Raemee chuckles awkwardly]

00:24:58.048 --> 00:24:59.842 line:80%
-Take this.
-Okay.

00:24:59.925 --> 00:25:01.135 line:80%
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-[Manjae chuckles]

00:25:01.218 --> 00:25:03.429 line:80%
Too bad. Ribbons are my signature.

00:25:03.512 --> 00:25:05.306 line:80%
[Sol and Raemee laugh]

00:25:05.889 --> 00:25:09.184 line:80%
You brought coffee for everyone
since it'll be too obvious, right?

00:25:09.268 --> 00:25:10.519 line:80%
-[Manjae] Oh…
-[Haran chuckles]

00:25:10.602 --> 00:25:12.354 line:80%
-Could you tell?
-Yes.

00:25:12.438 --> 00:25:14.189 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:25:14.815 --> 00:25:16.400 line:80%
How was your trip to Chuncheon?

00:25:16.483 --> 00:25:18.694 line:80%
Grandma was so excited to go.

00:25:18.777 --> 00:25:21.447 line:80%
Uh… Of course.

00:25:21.530 --> 00:25:22.614 line:80%
We had a great time.

00:25:24.033 --> 00:25:26.452 line:80%
By the way, is Mr. Seonu okay?

00:25:26.535 --> 00:25:28.537 line:80%
I didn't call
since I didn't want to bother him.

00:25:28.620 --> 00:25:31.248 line:80%
What? Did something happen?

00:25:31.832 --> 00:25:35.085 line:80%
He clearly doesn't seem well,
but he won't tell me.

00:25:37.921 --> 00:25:40.549 line:80%
Some people have a hard time

00:25:40.632 --> 00:25:43.052 line:80%
sharing things when they care
about someone deeply.

00:25:45.179 --> 00:25:46.680 line:80%
I can guarantee you

00:25:47.222 --> 00:25:51.143 line:80%
that when Chan
really has to tell you something,

00:25:51.226 --> 00:25:52.853 line:80%
he'll tell you honestly

00:25:53.729 --> 00:25:55.272 line:80%
without hiding it.

00:25:55.356 --> 00:25:56.482 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:25:56.565 --> 00:26:00.152 line:80%
So just trust him
and wait patiently for that moment.

00:26:02.404 --> 00:26:03.405 line:80%
All right.

00:26:05.199 --> 00:26:06.200 line:80%
Mmm.

00:26:09.828 --> 00:26:11.580 line:80%
I startled you in Chuncheon, didn't I?

00:26:12.164 --> 00:26:14.792 line:80%
I was startled too and acted like a child.

00:26:14.875 --> 00:26:15.876 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:26:15.959 --> 00:26:18.545 line:80%
But you don't have to worry.

00:26:19.505 --> 00:26:21.131 line:80%
I already planned everything.

00:26:21.215 --> 00:26:23.634 line:80%
What plan? To disappear on your own?

00:26:25.469 --> 00:26:26.970 line:80%
Your checkup's tomorrow, right?

00:26:28.180 --> 00:26:30.349 line:80%
You have to take me with you.

00:26:31.225 --> 00:26:33.644 line:80%
How did you know the date?

00:26:33.727 --> 00:26:35.270 line:80%
I met Yougyum.

00:26:35.354 --> 00:26:39.274 line:80%
He told me about the necklace
and how he's the only one who knows.

00:26:39.358 --> 00:26:40.734 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:26:41.527 --> 00:26:42.695 line:80%
I see.

00:26:42.778 --> 00:26:46.407 line:80%
But I'm not a child, you know.

00:26:46.490 --> 00:26:48.742 line:80%
-I can go by myself--
-Nabong.

00:26:49.868 --> 00:26:52.788 line:80%
You don't have to act tough
in front of me.

00:26:54.873 --> 00:26:55.916 line:80%
I told you,

00:26:57.251 --> 00:26:59.253 line:80%
I won't let you be alone.

00:27:00.963 --> 00:27:02.381 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:27:03.590 --> 00:27:04.758 line:80%
I guess this is why

00:27:06.260 --> 00:27:07.761 line:80%
we met after 50 years.

00:27:09.513 --> 00:27:12.433 line:80%
You have no one to rely on,
and have so many things to protect.

00:27:15.185 --> 00:27:16.395 line:80%
I'll protect you,

00:27:18.105 --> 00:27:19.189 line:80%
so you can rely on me.

00:27:20.190 --> 00:27:21.859 line:80%
I'll stay by your side.

00:27:27.573 --> 00:27:28.574 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:27:28.657 --> 00:27:29.658 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:27:36.290 --> 00:27:37.374 line:80%
Hmm?

00:27:39.918 --> 00:27:42.046 line:80%
-What is all this?
-[cellphone vibrates]

00:27:44.882 --> 00:27:47.509 line:80%
[Nana] <i>You have to handle</i>
<i>everything on the desk in my place.</i>

00:27:47.593 --> 00:27:48.635 line:80%
<i>Finish them by today.</i>

00:27:48.719 --> 00:27:51.263 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[line connects, rings]

00:27:51.347 --> 00:27:52.806 line:80%
Hello? Ms. Kim--

00:27:52.890 --> 00:27:55.768 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Among the 12 SS candidate outfits,</i>
<i>the six I picked are fixed.</i>

00:27:55.851 --> 00:27:57.895 line:80%
<i>Pick the other six.</i>

00:27:57.978 --> 00:28:01.440 line:80%
<i>Submit a report on which to pick</i>
<i>and the reasons by today.</i>

00:28:01.523 --> 00:28:02.941 line:80%
What? But--

00:28:03.025 --> 00:28:05.152 line:80%
<i>You saw the pigment samples</i>
<i>yesterday, right?</i>

00:28:05.235 --> 00:28:08.155 line:80%
<i>Organize the differences in color</i>
<i>and decide which one to go with.</i>

00:28:08.238 --> 00:28:10.783 line:80%
<i>And the differences by fabric.</i>
<i>Send it by today.</i>

00:28:10.866 --> 00:28:12.534 line:80%
[sighs] Wait, Ms. Kim. I--

00:28:12.618 --> 00:28:15.496 line:80%
<i>I received two drafts</i>
<i>of the press kit for Paris.</i>

00:28:15.579 --> 00:28:18.374 line:80%
<i>Choose the one that suits our image</i>
<i>and give it to Mr. Yeon.</i>

00:28:18.457 --> 00:28:21.335 line:80%
<i>I have work outside the office,</i>
<i>so I won't be there today.</i>

00:28:21.418 --> 00:28:23.837 line:80%
<i>Finish everything by today</i>
<i>and send it to me by email.</i>

00:28:23.921 --> 00:28:26.965 line:80%
-All of that by today?
<i>-Are you saying you can't?</i>

00:28:27.049 --> 00:28:28.801 line:80%
<i>Did you forget?</i>
<i>I told you to take my workload.</i>

00:28:28.884 --> 00:28:30.386 line:80%
-[sighs] But still, this is…
-[line disconnects]

00:28:34.056 --> 00:28:35.140 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:28:36.016 --> 00:28:37.101 line:80%
Mr. Park!

00:28:41.605 --> 00:28:42.606 line:80%
[sighs]

00:28:44.858 --> 00:28:47.778 line:80%
Hmm? [inhales sharply]
He didn't mention anything.

00:28:49.405 --> 00:28:50.406 line:80%
Genius.

00:28:52.533 --> 00:28:54.952 line:80%
Do you know where Mr. Park went?

00:28:56.078 --> 00:28:57.079 line:80%
Hmm?

00:28:58.205 --> 00:29:00.040 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Where did he go?

00:29:02.292 --> 00:29:05.879 line:80%
Ms. Kim, can you confirm the materials…

00:29:06.505 --> 00:29:07.506 line:80%
Ah…

00:29:07.589 --> 00:29:09.258 line:80%
Right, she's at a meeting.

00:29:09.341 --> 00:29:10.384 line:80%
[in English] Okay.

00:29:11.510 --> 00:29:13.637 line:80%
-[objects clatter]
-[gasps]

00:29:13.721 --> 00:29:16.515 line:80%
[in Korean] I can't believe this.
Hayeong, you klutz.

00:29:19.310 --> 00:29:20.352 line:80%
Goodness.

00:29:21.103 --> 00:29:22.104 line:80%
What is this?

00:29:25.357 --> 00:29:27.860 line:80%
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE FOR MY GRANDDAUGHTERS
I'M STILL OKAY

00:29:27.943 --> 00:29:29.778 line:80%
KEEP GLASSES IN FRONT OF THE MONITOR

00:29:29.862 --> 00:29:31.822 line:80%
DON'T TAKE OFF YOUGYUM'S NECKLACE!

00:29:31.905 --> 00:29:33.449 line:80%
[♪ intriguing music playing]

00:29:34.658 --> 00:29:37.286 line:80%
"Noble Life Center"?

00:29:45.252 --> 00:29:47.212 line:20%
NOBLE LIFE CENTER
COUNSELING CENTER

00:29:51.800 --> 00:29:53.052 line:80%
[automation] <i>Secure retirement.</i>

00:29:53.135 --> 00:29:56.305 line:80%
<i>This is the Noble Life Center,</i>
<i>Korea's premium senior care center.</i>

00:29:57.014 --> 00:29:59.391 line:80%
[staff] <i>Hello, this is Noble Life Center.</i>

00:30:00.517 --> 00:30:02.436 line:80%
I…

00:30:04.188 --> 00:30:05.189 line:80%
[hesitates] I mean,

00:30:06.732 --> 00:30:07.733 line:80%
I wanted

00:30:08.567 --> 00:30:12.154 line:80%
to check my reservation.

00:30:12.237 --> 00:30:13.405 line:80%
[staff] <i>What is your name?</i>

00:30:15.658 --> 00:30:18.994 line:80%
I'm Kim Nabong's guardian.

00:30:19.078 --> 00:30:20.621 line:80%
[staff] <i>Right, Kim Nabong.</i>

00:30:20.704 --> 00:30:23.290 line:80%
<i>She's still set to move in</i>
<i>at the end of June, right?</i>

00:30:24.041 --> 00:30:25.918 line:80%
<i>You wanted a single room</i>

00:30:26.001 --> 00:30:28.462 line:80%
<i>and signed up for the specialized</i>
<i>dementia care, right?</i>

00:30:28.545 --> 00:30:31.215 line:80%
CLOSET KEY, JEWELRY BOX

00:30:32.132 --> 00:30:33.801 line:80%
"Closet key, jewelry box…"

00:30:46.981 --> 00:30:49.441 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:30:49.525 --> 00:30:51.694 line:80%
[Haran] I really don't need lunch.

00:30:51.777 --> 00:30:54.655 line:80%
[exclaims softly]
When do I finish all of this?

00:31:00.160 --> 00:31:01.412 line:80%
Hayeong.

00:31:04.581 --> 00:31:05.874 line:80%
What is it?

00:31:05.958 --> 00:31:07.835 line:80%
What's wrong? Huh?

00:31:08.919 --> 00:31:10.838 line:80%
[sniffles] What do we do?

00:31:11.588 --> 00:31:13.799 line:80%
[sobbing] What do we do about Grandma?

00:31:14.383 --> 00:31:16.677 line:80%
What about Grandma? What's going on?

00:31:16.760 --> 00:31:18.762 line:80%
[♪ somber music playing]

00:31:21.140 --> 00:31:22.349 line:80%
[stutters] What is this?

00:31:27.813 --> 00:31:30.441 line:80%
NOBLE LIFE CENTER
CALL TO CONFIRM RESERVATION ON THE 17TH!

00:31:35.487 --> 00:31:37.156 line:80%
[Hadam panting]

00:31:37.948 --> 00:31:40.659 line:80%
What do you mean?
Why would she go to a care center?

00:31:41.994 --> 00:31:45.664 line:80%
I know you're just playing a joke
since my CSAT is over.

00:31:45.748 --> 00:31:48.083 line:80%
-Hadam.
-That doesn't make any sense.

00:31:48.876 --> 00:31:50.127 line:80%
Why would Grandma…

00:31:50.669 --> 00:31:53.297 line:80%
[yells] Why would she go there?
[breathing heavily]

00:31:53.380 --> 00:31:56.592 line:80%
[sighs] I think she was trying
to leave quietly.

00:31:58.552 --> 00:32:00.262 line:80%
[Hayeong] She must have been planning it

00:32:01.013 --> 00:32:02.890 line:80%
for quite a long time.

00:32:07.394 --> 00:32:09.355 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:32:18.030 --> 00:32:20.032 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:33.545 line:80%
This was in here.

00:32:46.100 --> 00:32:48.018 line:80%
[Nana] <i>To my beloved granddaughters.</i>

00:32:48.602 --> 00:32:52.272 line:80%
<i>Bonjour, my beautiful granddaughters</i>
<i>who took after me.</i>

00:32:52.356 --> 00:32:54.400 line:80%
<i>By the time you've opened this,</i>

00:32:54.483 --> 00:32:57.277 line:80%
<i>I'll probably be having champagne</i>

00:32:57.361 --> 00:32:59.363 line:80%
<i>on a plane to southern France.</i>

00:33:00.447 --> 00:33:01.824 line:80%
[med tech] Don't move, ma'am.

00:33:01.907 --> 00:33:04.159 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Don't be too upset.</i>

00:33:04.785 --> 00:33:08.831 line:80%
<i>I want to reward myself</i>
<i>for working hard all these years.</i>

00:33:08.914 --> 00:33:10.749 line:80%
<i>So I'm really happy.</i>

00:33:10.833 --> 00:33:13.252 line:80%
-[nurse] Please curl your back.
-[Nana] <i>Oh.</i>

00:33:13.335 --> 00:33:16.422 line:80%
[Nana] <i>And don't try to visit me.</i>

00:33:16.505 --> 00:33:18.799 line:80%
<i>I had such a hard time in my 20s</i>

00:33:18.882 --> 00:33:21.218 line:80%
<i>attending fashion school</i>
<i>with a baby on my back.</i>

00:33:21.301 --> 00:33:23.178 line:80%
<i>And I didn't get to try so many things</i>

00:33:23.762 --> 00:33:26.598 line:80%
<i>because I had no money or time.</i>

00:33:27.099 --> 00:33:31.520 line:80%
<i>I'm going to be extremely busy</i>
<i>doing everything I couldn't do back then.</i>

00:33:32.438 --> 00:33:33.731 line:80%
<i>So please…</i>

00:33:33.814 --> 00:33:35.024 line:80%
-[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong.
-Yes.

00:33:35.107 --> 00:33:37.568 line:80%
-[Nana] <i>Let me enjoy my life here.</i>
-Head to the next room.

00:33:37.651 --> 00:33:41.822 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Ah. And as for those</i>
<i>wedding gowns…</i>

00:33:42.489 --> 00:33:44.783 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:33:51.582 --> 00:33:56.045 line:80%
<i>Your grandma's the famous Kim Nana,</i>

00:33:56.128 --> 00:33:59.173 line:80%
<i>so letting you wear wedding gowns</i>
<i>made by someone else?</i>

00:33:59.673 --> 00:34:00.966 line:80%
[in English] <i>Oh, no.</i>

00:34:01.050 --> 00:34:02.676 line:80%
[in Korean] <i>I can never let that happen.</i>

00:34:04.678 --> 00:34:07.723 line:80%
<i>I thought I'd be too busy</i>
<i>having fun in France</i>

00:34:07.806 --> 00:34:09.642 line:80%
<i>to make any clothes,</i>

00:34:09.725 --> 00:34:11.060 line:80%
<i>so I made them in advance.</i>

00:34:11.810 --> 00:34:15.147 line:80%
<i>I just made them easily in my spare time.</i>

00:34:17.608 --> 00:34:20.235 line:80%
<i>Let's meet again someday</i>

00:34:20.319 --> 00:34:22.613 line:80%
<i>after shining in each of our places.</i>

00:34:23.322 --> 00:34:27.743 line:80%
<i>I'll be rooting for your glorious lives</i>
<i>from far away.</i>

00:34:28.535 --> 00:34:29.620 line:80%
<i>Haran,</i>

00:34:29.703 --> 00:34:31.288 line:80%
<i>Hayeong,</i>

00:34:32.122 --> 00:34:33.207 line:80%
<i>Hadam.</i>

00:34:37.836 --> 00:34:40.047 line:80%
<i>My life was a brilliant shade of rose</i>

00:34:40.714 --> 00:34:45.094 line:80%
<i>because you three were my granddaughters.</i>

00:34:46.428 --> 00:34:47.429 line:80%
<i>Take care.</i>

00:34:47.930 --> 00:34:48.931 line:80%
[in French] <i>Au revoir.</i>

00:34:49.974 --> 00:34:50.975 line:80%
<i>Ah.</i>

00:34:51.058 --> 00:34:55.562 line:80%
[in Korean] <i>I hate saying cheesy things,</i>
<i>but I'm the type to say things I need to.</i>

00:34:55.646 --> 00:34:56.855 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:34:56.939 --> 00:34:57.940 line:80%
<i>I love you,</i>

00:34:58.607 --> 00:35:00.567 line:80%
<i>my dear granddaughters.</i>

00:35:02.987 --> 00:35:04.196 line:80%
[Hadam] <i>Why…</i>

00:35:04.697 --> 00:35:05.698 line:80%
[Haran sighs]

00:35:05.781 --> 00:35:07.825 line:80%
She has three granddaughters.

00:35:09.076 --> 00:35:10.244 line:80%
Why would she…

00:35:10.327 --> 00:35:11.996 line:80%
It's weird that she's at a meeting.

00:35:13.163 --> 00:35:14.415 line:80%
Where is she right now?

00:35:15.582 --> 00:35:17.126 line:80%
She hasn't left already, has she?

00:35:18.752 --> 00:35:19.753 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:35:26.301 --> 00:35:29.513 line:80%
SECRET WITH YOUGYUM
DON'T TAKE OFF YOUGYUM'S NECKLACE!

00:35:29.596 --> 00:35:30.806 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:35:30.889 --> 00:35:33.142 line:80%
Why don't you spend some time
with your grandma--

00:35:33.225 --> 00:35:35.602 line:80%
Why are you suddenly
bringing up my grandma?

00:35:35.686 --> 00:35:36.687 line:80%
What?

00:35:37.646 --> 00:35:38.647 line:80%
Oh…

00:35:38.731 --> 00:35:41.692 line:80%
Why was your tumbler
in my grandma's study?

00:35:41.775 --> 00:35:43.485 line:80%
I ran into her a while ago in the park.

00:35:43.569 --> 00:35:45.696 line:80%
You know she wouldn't do such a thing.

00:35:52.953 --> 00:35:56.665 line:80%
[breath trembling] Cha Yougyum.
You knew about Grandma, didn't you?

00:35:57.291 --> 00:35:58.542 line:80%
Where is she right now?

00:35:58.625 --> 00:36:01.962 line:80%
[yelling] I already know everything!
Just tell me! [breathing heavily]

00:36:03.213 --> 00:36:05.466 line:80%
[Yougyum] <i>She's getting a checkup today.</i>

00:36:12.765 --> 00:36:13.766 line:80%
Over there.

00:36:13.849 --> 00:36:15.768 line:80%
NEUROLOGY CENTER

00:36:19.938 --> 00:36:21.732 line:80%
-[Manjae] Oh.
-Hey, Manjae.

00:36:21.815 --> 00:36:23.525 line:80%
-That took a while, didn't it?
-[Manjae] Goodness.

00:36:23.651 --> 00:36:24.860 line:80%
You did great.

00:36:24.943 --> 00:36:26.236 line:80%
-Are you okay?
-[Nana] Yes.

00:36:26.320 --> 00:36:28.322 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:36:32.701 --> 00:36:34.078 line:80%
[sighs]

00:36:34.161 --> 00:36:35.537 line:80%
How can you…

00:36:35.621 --> 00:36:37.706 line:80%
Of all people, how can you do this to me?

00:36:37.790 --> 00:36:39.333 line:80%
Why are you--

00:36:39.416 --> 00:36:41.251 line:80%
You should take some of my workload.

00:36:41.335 --> 00:36:43.045 line:80%
<i>Let me get some rest, too.</i>

00:36:43.128 --> 00:36:45.589 line:80%
He's not keeping it from you.
He probably can't.

00:36:45.673 --> 00:36:48.384 line:80%
He probably doesn't want
to burden you with his pain.

00:36:48.467 --> 00:36:51.095 line:80%
<i>He cares more about protecting you</i>
<i>than his own pain.</i>

00:36:52.304 --> 00:36:53.305 line:80%
[sighs]

00:36:57.518 --> 00:36:58.727 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>A meeting?</i>

00:36:58.811 --> 00:37:00.229 line:80%
And what's this…

00:37:00.312 --> 00:37:01.313 line:80%
I'll do it.

00:37:07.319 --> 00:37:08.404 line:80%
[Hadam] <i>What was that, Grandma?</i>

00:37:08.487 --> 00:37:10.739 line:80%
You didn't even look at him
and didn't say a word.

00:37:10.823 --> 00:37:12.992 line:80%
He left because
you made him uncomfortable.

00:37:13.075 --> 00:37:16.078 line:80%
Did Grandma summon you
and threaten you or something?

00:37:16.662 --> 00:37:19.081 line:80%
[breathes deeply, sighs]

00:37:19.623 --> 00:37:21.542 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:37:28.340 --> 00:37:30.300 line:80%
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE FOR MY GRANDDAUGHTERS

00:37:43.272 --> 00:37:44.273 line:80%
[Hadam] Grandma.

00:37:52.781 --> 00:37:53.907 line:80%
[Nana] I'm okay.

00:37:54.491 --> 00:37:55.492 line:80%
It's all right.

00:37:58.746 --> 00:38:01.123 line:80%
[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong.
Please go to the next room.

00:38:01.206 --> 00:38:02.249 line:80%
[Manjae] Okay.

00:38:03.542 --> 00:38:04.835 line:80%
I'll be back.

00:38:04.918 --> 00:38:06.003 line:80%
[Manjae] Let's go.

00:38:07.463 --> 00:38:09.590 line:80%
-[Haran sighs worriedly]
-[Manjae mumbles]

00:38:11.884 --> 00:38:12.926 line:80%
[sighs]

00:38:15.721 --> 00:38:18.057 line:80%
-[Nana sniffles]
-[Manjae] You've a lot of granddaughters.

00:38:18.140 --> 00:38:19.558 line:80%
All right.

00:38:19.642 --> 00:38:20.643 line:80%
See you in a bit.

00:38:23.729 --> 00:38:24.938 line:80%
[Hayeong sighs wearily]

00:38:32.863 --> 00:38:33.864 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:38:33.947 --> 00:38:35.949 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:38:36.659 --> 00:38:40.537 line:80%
Make sure to keep it dry,
and tell me if it's too tight.

00:38:40.621 --> 00:38:41.872 line:80%
Okay. Thank you.

00:38:43.791 --> 00:38:44.792 line:80%
[Changmo] Are you okay?

00:38:44.875 --> 00:38:46.377 line:80%
[grunts] I'm fine.

00:38:47.544 --> 00:38:49.713 line:80%
You need some vitamins.
I'll peel these for you.

00:38:49.797 --> 00:38:52.091 line:80%
-It's fine, I'll do it.
-Mmm-mmm.

00:38:52.174 --> 00:38:54.426 line:80%
-Ah…
-[yells] Cha Yougyum!

00:38:55.177 --> 00:38:56.178 line:80%
[sighs]

00:38:57.137 --> 00:38:58.138 line:80%
Bye.

00:39:01.934 --> 00:39:02.935 line:80%
Hadam…

00:39:05.688 --> 00:39:08.065 line:80%
I'm sorry I didn't tell you
about your grandma.

00:39:08.148 --> 00:39:09.817 line:80%
She said…

00:39:13.529 --> 00:39:15.572 line:80%
Thank you, Yougyum. [sobbing]

00:39:15.656 --> 00:39:16.657 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:39:16.740 --> 00:39:18.158 line:80%
Thank you so much.

00:39:19.284 --> 00:39:22.371 line:80%
[Manjae]
<i>Yougyum has been taking care of her.</i>

00:39:22.454 --> 00:39:24.164 line:80%
<i>Without the necklace he gave her,</i>

00:39:24.248 --> 00:39:27.084 line:80%
<i>I would've lost her in Chuncheon.</i>

00:39:28.210 --> 00:39:31.755 line:80%
<i>It must have been tough</i>
<i>keeping that secret on his own.</i>

00:39:32.464 --> 00:39:35.050 line:80%
She would've had a hard time on her own.

00:39:36.844 --> 00:39:37.845 line:80%
Thank you

00:39:38.595 --> 00:39:40.264 line:80%
for taking care of her.

00:39:46.645 --> 00:39:47.980 line:80%
Sorry, I didn't tell you.

00:39:48.522 --> 00:39:49.940 line:80%
You must've been shocked.

00:39:51.358 --> 00:39:52.359 line:80%
Thank you.

00:39:53.694 --> 00:39:56.113 line:80%
Thank you so, so much, Yougyum.

00:40:00.159 --> 00:40:02.786 line:80%
Let's go see her.

00:40:04.038 --> 00:40:06.040 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:40:06.123 --> 00:40:08.125 line:80%
[panting]

00:40:24.099 --> 00:40:25.100 line:80%
[Taeseok] I didn't know.

00:40:27.353 --> 00:40:29.313 line:80%
I should've known,

00:40:30.981 --> 00:40:31.982 line:80%
but I didn't.

00:40:32.650 --> 00:40:33.651 line:80%
Why?

00:40:34.193 --> 00:40:36.236 line:80%
How could you not know?

00:40:36.987 --> 00:40:39.448 line:80%
It was you of all people.

00:40:39.531 --> 00:40:41.033 line:80%
You said she was your savior,

00:40:41.867 --> 00:40:43.494 line:80%
and you promised to take care of her.

00:40:43.577 --> 00:40:45.913 line:80%
You were always by her side.
How could you not know?

00:40:45.996 --> 00:40:47.790 line:80%
[♪ melancholic music playing]

00:40:47.873 --> 00:40:50.542 line:80%
When I asked if anything happened
in Seongsu-dong,

00:40:51.377 --> 00:40:52.670 line:80%
why did you hide it from me?

00:40:53.545 --> 00:40:55.798 line:80%
No, if you weren't going to tell me,

00:40:55.881 --> 00:40:58.008 line:80%
shouldn't you have
looked into it more, at least?

00:40:58.092 --> 00:40:59.968 line:80%
If you'd found out then…

00:41:00.886 --> 00:41:01.887 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:41:03.055 --> 00:41:04.056 line:80%
[Hayeong] No.

00:41:04.890 --> 00:41:06.308 line:80%
Pretend you didn't hear that.

00:41:07.267 --> 00:41:08.686 line:80%
What I just said

00:41:09.478 --> 00:41:11.647 line:80%
is actually what I want to say to myself.

00:41:13.899 --> 00:41:16.110 line:80%
I know it's not your fault,

00:41:16.694 --> 00:41:20.781 line:80%
but I feel so pathetic and stupid.

00:41:22.282 --> 00:41:24.535 line:80%
So I don't know what to do.

00:41:25.786 --> 00:41:27.997 line:80%
I should've known.

00:41:29.206 --> 00:41:30.207 line:80%
I'm sorry…

00:41:31.083 --> 00:41:32.334 line:80%
I yelled at you.

00:41:41.427 --> 00:41:42.428 line:80%
[breath trembling]

00:41:43.554 --> 00:41:44.596 line:80%
Sorry.

00:41:44.680 --> 00:41:45.681 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:41:46.598 --> 00:41:48.600 line:80%
[line connects, rings]

00:41:51.395 --> 00:41:52.563 line:80%
He's not picking up.

00:41:53.564 --> 00:41:55.357 line:80%
Mr. Park, where are you?

00:41:55.441 --> 00:41:58.193 line:80%
Customers are coming in,
asking why you're closed today.

00:42:00.571 --> 00:42:01.572 line:80%
The hospital?

00:42:03.657 --> 00:42:04.992 line:80%
Then what about…

00:42:05.075 --> 00:42:07.244 line:80%
What about Ms. Song?

00:42:07.870 --> 00:42:10.956 line:80%
[doctor] The MRI shows
normal intracranial pressure,

00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:14.043 line:80%
but the ventricles
are significantly enlarged.

00:42:14.126 --> 00:42:16.712 line:80%
We also ran a cerebrospinal fluid test
to double-check,

00:42:16.795 --> 00:42:18.339 line:80%
and the results show…

00:42:20.966 --> 00:42:22.217 line:80%
that it's not dementia.

00:42:23.427 --> 00:42:24.970 line:80%
-Really?
-[all sigh in relief]

00:42:25.054 --> 00:42:26.305 line:80%
[Hayeong whispers] That's such a relief.

00:42:26.388 --> 00:42:30.267 line:80%
But we suspect
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

00:42:30.351 --> 00:42:31.935 line:80%
Hydrocephalus?

00:42:32.019 --> 00:42:34.813 line:80%
It occurs when cerebrospinal fluid
isn't properly absorbed,

00:42:34.897 --> 00:42:38.651 line:80%
leading to symptoms like memory loss
and problems with walking.

00:42:38.734 --> 00:42:41.612 line:80%
The symptoms are similar,
so some mistake it for dementia.

00:42:41.695 --> 00:42:42.946 line:80%
I see.

00:42:43.030 --> 00:42:45.866 line:80%
Have you had any problems
with walking recently?

00:42:46.992 --> 00:42:49.745 line:80%
-I don't think I've seen…
-I'm not sure…

00:42:50.245 --> 00:42:51.372 line:80%
-[Yougyum exclaims] Oh!
-[Manjae] Oh gosh.

00:42:51.455 --> 00:42:55.084 line:80%
She did. Last time,
you had bruises on your legs.

00:42:55.167 --> 00:42:57.294 line:80%
Huh? Did you hit your leg somewhere?

00:42:57.378 --> 00:43:00.130 line:80%
It's fine. I just fell.
My legs suddenly wouldn't listen.

00:43:00.881 --> 00:43:03.300 line:80%
[doctor] <i>Patients usually show a response</i>
<i>within 24 hours,</i>

00:43:03.384 --> 00:43:06.011 line:80%
<i>even within 10 hours</i>
<i>after draining the cerebrospinal fluid.</i>

00:43:06.095 --> 00:43:08.555 line:80%
<i>We'll be able to confirm this</i>
<i>after the gait test.</i>

00:43:08.639 --> 00:43:10.891 line:80%
<i>So let's see</i>
<i>how much improvement there is.</i>

00:43:11.684 --> 00:43:14.353 line:80%
You can see how you sometimes
had narrower strides

00:43:14.436 --> 00:43:16.981 line:80%
and dragged your feet
in the morning, right?

00:43:17.064 --> 00:43:19.608 line:80%
But it improved significantly
after draining the fluid.

00:43:20.651 --> 00:43:23.612 line:80%
The tap test confirms
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

00:43:23.696 --> 00:43:27.241 line:80%
[inhales sharply] She can get better
with treatment, right?

00:43:27.324 --> 00:43:29.118 line:80%
With successful surgery,
she should improve.

00:43:29.201 --> 00:43:30.619 line:80%
[Manjae] All right.

00:43:30.703 --> 00:43:33.038 line:80%
We'll create a small opening in the skull

00:43:33.122 --> 00:43:35.958 line:80%
and insert a thin tube called a shunt
into the ventricle

00:43:36.041 --> 00:43:39.545 line:80%
to drain excess cerebrospinal fluid
into the abdomen.

00:43:39.628 --> 00:43:41.130 line:80%
Ah…

00:43:41.213 --> 00:43:44.383 line:80%
[doctor] Given your age, I suggest
getting hospitalized a few days in advance

00:43:44.466 --> 00:43:46.135 line:80%
to run some basic tests first.

00:43:46.802 --> 00:43:48.220 line:80%
Proceed with the admission,

00:43:48.303 --> 00:43:51.557 line:80%
and we'll set the surgery date
based on your condition.

00:43:51.640 --> 00:43:53.100 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:43:53.183 --> 00:43:55.602 line:80%
The admission's done already?

00:43:55.686 --> 00:44:00.149 line:80%
Yes, a tall man in a suit
came and finished the process.

00:44:00.232 --> 00:44:01.734 line:80%
He even paid the fees.

00:44:02.401 --> 00:44:03.610 line:80%
[sighs]

00:44:05.571 --> 00:44:06.655 line:80%
[Hayeong] Mr. Yeon.

00:44:06.739 --> 00:44:09.033 line:80%
[panting]

00:44:30.346 --> 00:44:32.348 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:44:32.931 --> 00:44:33.974 line:80%
Cha Yougyum.

00:44:34.058 --> 00:44:35.059 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim.

00:44:35.142 --> 00:44:38.979 line:80%
You're an athlete.
Go take care of your own condition.

00:44:39.063 --> 00:44:40.230 line:80%
You need to recover.

00:44:40.314 --> 00:44:42.149 line:80%
-Song Hadam.
-Yes?

00:44:42.775 --> 00:44:44.068 line:80%
You said you'd help him.

00:44:44.568 --> 00:44:46.362 line:80%
Stay right by his side.

00:44:47.363 --> 00:44:48.405 line:80%
And…

00:44:49.531 --> 00:44:51.033 line:80%
Song Haran, Song Hayeong.

00:44:51.116 --> 00:44:55.079 line:80%
No, Lead Designer Song,
Designer Song Hayeong.

00:44:55.162 --> 00:44:59.833 line:80%
If anything at my company
goes wrong while I'm away,

00:44:59.917 --> 00:45:01.251 line:80%
I'm kicking all of you out.

00:45:01.335 --> 00:45:03.045 line:80%
So focus on work from now on.

00:45:03.128 --> 00:45:05.297 line:80%
Don't even think about coming here.

00:45:05.381 --> 00:45:06.674 line:80%
-But…
-[Manjae claps]

00:45:07.257 --> 00:45:08.258 line:80%
[in English] Okay.

00:45:08.342 --> 00:45:11.011 line:80%
[in Korean] I'll be taking care of her
from now on,

00:45:11.095 --> 00:45:14.473 line:80%
so you youngsters
go and focus on your own stuff.

00:45:14.556 --> 00:45:16.850 line:80%
We'll take turns coming here.
You have your coffee shop.

00:45:16.934 --> 00:45:17.935 line:80%
[Manjae] Mmm-mmm.

00:45:18.018 --> 00:45:20.312 line:80%
SHIM is temporarily closed
until she gets surgery

00:45:20.396 --> 00:45:23.148 line:80%
and recovers well.

00:45:23.232 --> 00:45:24.692 line:80%
I'll think of this as winter vacation

00:45:24.775 --> 00:45:28.070 line:80%
and enjoy my time here with my old friend.

00:45:28.153 --> 00:45:29.279 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:45:29.363 --> 00:45:31.824 line:80%
All right. Everyone, stop bothering us.

00:45:32.908 --> 00:45:35.452 line:80%
But where did Mr. Yeon go?

00:45:35.536 --> 00:45:37.913 line:80%
-I thought I saw him in the hallway.
-[Haran] Oh.

00:45:37.997 --> 00:45:39.999 line:80%
He'll probably be busy
taking care of things

00:45:40.082 --> 00:45:41.625 line:80%
in Grandma's place.

00:45:45.087 --> 00:45:47.089 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:45:51.760 --> 00:45:52.803 line:80%
Oh?

00:45:55.097 --> 00:45:56.098 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:45:56.181 --> 00:45:58.684 line:80%
I'm sorry, I took so long.

00:45:59.351 --> 00:46:00.686 line:80%
How did you know?

00:46:00.769 --> 00:46:03.397 line:80%
I heard from Mr. Park just a while ago.

00:46:03.480 --> 00:46:06.108 line:80%
I'm sure her surgery will go well.

00:46:06.191 --> 00:46:07.359 line:80%
[sighs]

00:46:07.443 --> 00:46:12.990 line:80%
I wish the people I love won't feel pain,
physically or mentally.

00:46:13.574 --> 00:46:15.284 line:80%
I'm sure she'll overcome this.

00:46:15.367 --> 00:46:17.244 line:80%
So don't get too scared.

00:46:17.328 --> 00:46:18.662 line:80%
Everything will be all right.

00:46:19.204 --> 00:46:23.083 line:80%
[sighs] Sorry, but can we stay like this
for 10 more seconds?

00:46:23.167 --> 00:46:26.628 line:80%
We can stay like this for 10 minutes
or even 10 hours.

00:46:27.421 --> 00:46:29.965 line:80%
[sighs] Sorry,
I didn't contact you sooner.

00:46:30.049 --> 00:46:31.300 line:80%
Things were so hectic.

00:46:32.051 --> 00:46:33.052 line:80%
Oh?

00:46:34.303 --> 00:46:36.430 line:80%
I'll be upset if you feel sorry over this.

00:46:36.513 --> 00:46:38.140 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:46:38.223 --> 00:46:39.516 line:80%
You must've missed lunch.

00:46:40.309 --> 00:46:41.852 line:80%
Wait here, I'll get you something.

00:46:41.935 --> 00:46:45.939 line:80%
Then can I just get some coffee?
I don't think I can eat anything.

00:46:46.023 --> 00:46:47.816 line:80%
All right. Hang on.

00:46:48.400 --> 00:46:51.445 line:80%
[inhales sharply]
Why are you dressed so lightly?

00:46:53.238 --> 00:46:56.533 line:80%
This cardigan is really valuable to me,

00:46:56.617 --> 00:46:58.911 line:80%
so I don't usually lend it to anyone.

00:46:58.994 --> 00:47:00.996 line:80%
But I'll let you wear it just this once.

00:47:05.292 --> 00:47:06.293 line:80%
Don't ruin it.

00:47:10.172 --> 00:47:12.383 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:47:15.761 --> 00:47:16.970 line:80%
[footsteps approaching]

00:47:17.054 --> 00:47:18.055 line:80%
[Sujin] We meet again.

00:47:19.264 --> 00:47:20.849 line:80%
Oh. Hello.

00:47:21.433 --> 00:47:24.728 line:80%
My grandma's getting hospitalized here
for a few days.

00:47:24.812 --> 00:47:26.271 line:80%
Ah. Really?

00:47:26.814 --> 00:47:30.442 line:80%
Oh, um… I accidentally took
one of your bracelet charms.

00:47:30.526 --> 00:47:32.695 line:80%
I'll give it back to you
when I visit tomorrow.

00:47:32.778 --> 00:47:35.197 line:80%
Really? I was wondering
where that charm went.

00:47:35.280 --> 00:47:37.616 line:80%
That's great. But…

00:47:38.158 --> 00:47:39.952 line:80%
the man who was with you last time…

00:47:41.787 --> 00:47:43.163 line:80%
Is he your boyfriend?

00:47:43.998 --> 00:47:45.499 line:80%
Yes. Why do you ask?

00:47:45.582 --> 00:47:46.959 line:80%
You looked good together.

00:47:47.710 --> 00:47:50.796 line:80%
He reminded me of someone I used to know.

00:47:50.879 --> 00:47:52.589 line:80%
-Ah. [chuckles softly]
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:47:53.173 --> 00:47:55.634 line:20%
Oh… You're a neurology doctor.

00:47:56.510 --> 00:47:59.096 line:80%
My grandmother's getting surgery
for hydrocephalus.

00:47:59.179 --> 00:48:00.764 line:80%
Please take good care of her.

00:48:00.848 --> 00:48:03.767 line:80%
I'm only visiting, so I'm not authorized
to treat patients directly.

00:48:06.353 --> 00:48:07.563 line:80%
I came from Boston.

00:48:08.355 --> 00:48:09.356 line:80%
[Haran] Oh.

00:48:09.898 --> 00:48:11.191 line:80%
I see.

00:48:11.275 --> 00:48:13.027 line:80%
The neurosurgeons
will take good care of her.

00:48:13.110 --> 00:48:16.238 line:80%
The neurology department
will see the results, so I'll check.

00:48:16.822 --> 00:48:18.157 line:80%
And my bracelet…

00:48:18.866 --> 00:48:20.284 line:80%
I was worried

00:48:21.160 --> 00:48:23.954 line:80%
about the gap in my bracelet.

00:48:24.580 --> 00:48:26.915 line:80%
I'm glad you'll give it back to me.

00:48:26.999 --> 00:48:29.001 line:80%
-I'll see you tomorrow.
-All right.

00:48:30.127 --> 00:48:31.128 line:80%
Bye.

00:48:34.673 --> 00:48:35.716 line:80%
You're back.

00:48:37.259 --> 00:48:39.678 line:80%
[cellphone vibrating]

00:48:41.513 --> 00:48:42.973 line:80%
Yes, Mr. Park.

00:48:43.057 --> 00:48:45.517 line:80%
Oh, I met Mr. Seonu in the lobby.

00:48:45.601 --> 00:48:46.935 line:80%
Really?

00:48:47.603 --> 00:48:48.604 line:80%
Okay.

00:48:48.687 --> 00:48:52.274 line:80%
Grandma said
she wants to talk to you alone.

00:48:52.358 --> 00:48:53.692 line:80%
Is that okay?

00:48:53.776 --> 00:48:56.695 line:80%
-If you feel uncomfortable…
-[chuckles softly] No, it's fine.

00:48:58.072 --> 00:49:00.074 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:49:00.699 --> 00:49:03.535 line:80%
I should have put more thought
into what you said that day.

00:49:03.619 --> 00:49:05.245 line:80%
I'm sorry, Ms. Kim.

00:49:05.329 --> 00:49:06.664 line:80%
"That day"?

00:49:06.747 --> 00:49:08.916 line:80%
Thanks to you,
I'll be able to leave in peace.

00:49:08.999 --> 00:49:10.376 line:80%
Are you going somewhere?

00:49:11.502 --> 00:49:14.505 line:80%
I'm planning to stay in France
after I retire.

00:49:17.716 --> 00:49:19.843 line:80%
I hid this on purpose.

00:49:20.469 --> 00:49:22.137 line:80%
How could you have known?

00:49:24.306 --> 00:49:25.307 line:80%
Are you all right?

00:49:25.891 --> 00:49:27.267 line:80%
I'm fine.

00:49:28.894 --> 00:49:29.895 line:80%
But…

00:49:30.437 --> 00:49:32.231 line:80%
I'd like to ask you the same thing.

00:49:32.314 --> 00:49:33.732 line:80%
I heard about your head.

00:49:34.942 --> 00:49:36.276 line:80%
Are you sure you're okay?

00:49:37.820 --> 00:49:38.821 line:80%
I'm fine.

00:49:39.738 --> 00:49:40.781 line:80%
No,

00:49:40.864 --> 00:49:43.033 line:80%
I'm going to make sure I'm fine

00:49:43.701 --> 00:49:45.953 line:80%
so I can stay by Ms. Song's side.

00:49:46.829 --> 00:49:48.956 line:80%
My head, and everything else…

00:49:51.500 --> 00:49:52.835 line:80%
I'm going to make it all okay.

00:49:52.918 --> 00:49:54.920 line:80%
[♪ mellow music playing]

00:49:55.671 --> 00:49:56.672 line:80%
Haran cares…

00:49:58.173 --> 00:49:59.925 line:80%
for you a lot.

00:50:00.009 --> 00:50:03.095 line:80%
It actually surprised me
how sincere she is about you.

00:50:03.721 --> 00:50:06.807 line:80%
And she seems to be
thinking of a future with you.

00:50:08.058 --> 00:50:11.103 line:80%
I know, and I feel the same way.

00:50:11.186 --> 00:50:12.563 line:80%
[Nana] I want to see you two

00:50:13.981 --> 00:50:16.442 line:80%
getting along well for as long as I can.

00:50:17.693 --> 00:50:21.155 line:80%
At least for Haran's sake and your sake,

00:50:22.656 --> 00:50:24.033 line:80%
make sure you're okay.

00:50:27.870 --> 00:50:28.871 line:80%
I will.

00:50:32.499 --> 00:50:34.126 line:80%
Thanks for coming.

00:50:34.209 --> 00:50:36.795 line:80%
Oh. When's your checkup again?

00:50:36.879 --> 00:50:37.880 line:80%
Next week.

00:50:37.963 --> 00:50:40.090 line:80%
It'll be fine, so don't worry about me.

00:50:40.174 --> 00:50:41.508 line:80%
Take good care of Ms. Kim.

00:50:42.092 --> 00:50:43.093 line:80%
I'll get going now.

00:50:43.177 --> 00:50:44.845 line:80%
-Right, your cardigan.
-Ah…

00:50:45.846 --> 00:50:47.514 line:80%
Keep it on. You'll catch a cold.

00:50:50.017 --> 00:50:51.226 line:80%
Don't worry.

00:50:55.230 --> 00:50:56.690 line:80%
Grandma was right.

00:50:57.816 --> 00:51:01.445 line:80%
Having just one person to lean on

00:51:01.528 --> 00:51:02.905 line:80%
will help you stay strong.

00:51:04.990 --> 00:51:06.950 line:80%
[inhales sharply, exclaims boastfully]

00:51:07.034 --> 00:51:09.662 line:80%
I do have a pretty broad back.

00:51:09.745 --> 00:51:10.996 line:80%
When did you notice?

00:51:11.080 --> 00:51:13.332 line:80%
Should I leave my back here
for you to lean on?

00:51:13.415 --> 00:51:14.416 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:51:15.751 --> 00:51:18.337 line:80%
-Go. [chuckling]
-Okay. I'll go now.

00:51:18.420 --> 00:51:19.421 line:80%
Bye.

00:51:22.966 --> 00:51:24.051 line:80%
Head back inside.

00:51:27.721 --> 00:51:29.723 line:80%
[footsteps receding]

00:51:30.349 --> 00:51:31.350 line:80%
[sighs]

00:51:44.321 --> 00:51:45.322 line:80%
Let me talk to you.

00:51:46.615 --> 00:51:48.033 line:80%
What do you think you're doing?

00:51:48.117 --> 00:51:49.743 line:80%
Stop messing with her.

00:51:49.827 --> 00:51:51.495 line:80%
The thing you wanted to protect…

00:51:53.038 --> 00:51:54.039 line:80%
was her?

00:51:54.748 --> 00:51:57.126 line:80%
Are you worried you'll lose her
if I say something?

00:51:58.127 --> 00:51:59.378 line:80%
Does she know

00:51:59.461 --> 00:52:02.881 line:80%
that you went to the same school
as Hyeokchan and were his roommate?

00:52:02.965 --> 00:52:03.966 line:80%
Does she know who you are?

00:52:05.300 --> 00:52:08.012 line:80%
Hyeokchan's dead, but you're alive,

00:52:08.095 --> 00:52:10.681 line:80%
and the person you want to protect
is his old girlfriend?

00:52:11.849 --> 00:52:12.891 line:80%
That's funny.

00:52:12.975 --> 00:52:13.976 line:80%
Since when?

00:52:14.059 --> 00:52:15.728 line:80%
Did you have feelings for her then?

00:52:15.811 --> 00:52:17.771 line:80%
You must've jumped at the chance
when he died.

00:52:17.855 --> 00:52:19.565 line:80%
Don't say it like that.

00:52:19.648 --> 00:52:21.025 line:80%
That's not the case.

00:52:22.067 --> 00:52:25.070 line:80%
She's going through a hard time right now.

00:52:25.696 --> 00:52:27.990 line:80%
Don't say things that…

00:52:29.033 --> 00:52:30.409 line:80%
will only dig up old wounds.

00:52:30.492 --> 00:52:31.910 line:80%
Please.

00:52:31.994 --> 00:52:34.163 line:80%
Why should I do that for you?

00:52:35.164 --> 00:52:36.165 line:80%
[scoffs]

00:52:37.333 --> 00:52:38.500 line:80%
I remembered something.

00:52:39.376 --> 00:52:40.961 line:80%
The day that the waste container fell,

00:52:42.338 --> 00:52:44.089 line:80%
you were in the lab as well.

00:52:44.173 --> 00:52:45.758 line:80%
And you were shouting at him to stop.

00:52:45.841 --> 00:52:47.885 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:52:48.886 --> 00:52:52.014 line:80%
I don't have the time
to answer all your questions.

00:52:52.097 --> 00:52:54.683 line:80%
Why was the waste container
next to Hyeokchan?

00:52:56.935 --> 00:52:58.979 line:80%
The day Hyeokchan's lip was busted…

00:52:59.063 --> 00:53:00.147 line:80%
Was that day

00:53:00.856 --> 00:53:02.816 line:80%
the day of the accident?

00:53:04.026 --> 00:53:06.820 line:80%
I didn't have any memories
of that day until now,

00:53:06.904 --> 00:53:08.822 line:80%
but it feels like it's from that day.

00:53:08.906 --> 00:53:12.826 line:80%
Tell me what happened in the lab that day.

00:53:14.203 --> 00:53:15.204 line:80%
You know what happened.

00:53:16.914 --> 00:53:19.500 line:80%
You can't tell Haran the truth.

00:53:19.583 --> 00:53:20.834 line:80%
No, you're not telling her.

00:53:20.918 --> 00:53:23.545 line:80%
So why are you so obsessed
with finding out what happened?

00:53:23.629 --> 00:53:26.006 line:80%
If everyone involved
has the right to know,

00:53:26.090 --> 00:53:29.677 line:80%
shouldn't Haran also know
that you're fake?

00:53:30.636 --> 00:53:32.096 line:80%
I'm going to tell her.

00:53:32.179 --> 00:53:34.682 line:80%
-But right now--
-If you go and tell her first,

00:53:34.765 --> 00:53:37.476 line:80%
then I might think about telling you, too.

00:53:45.567 --> 00:53:46.652 line:80%
Please.

00:53:46.735 --> 00:53:48.779 line:80%
Stop asking me strange questions.

00:53:49.571 --> 00:53:50.864 line:80%
If you provoke me,

00:53:50.948 --> 00:53:54.493 line:80%
even I don't know
what I'll end up telling her.

00:54:02.459 --> 00:54:03.585 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Hey, Kang Hyeokchan.</i>

00:54:04.378 --> 00:54:05.921 line:80%
<i>I have to tell you something.</i>

00:54:06.005 --> 00:54:09.425 line:80%
I've been chatting with your girlfriend.

00:54:09.508 --> 00:54:11.260 line:80%
She thinks she's been talking to you.

00:54:11.844 --> 00:54:13.012 line:80%
You were pretending to be me?

00:54:13.095 --> 00:54:14.596 line:80%
Do you have any idea what you've done?

00:54:14.680 --> 00:54:15.931 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:54:16.015 --> 00:54:17.933 line:80%
-I'm sorry.
-[Sujin] <i>Did you have feelings for her?</i>

00:54:18.017 --> 00:54:19.643 line:80%
<i>You must've jumped at the chance.</i>

00:54:19.727 --> 00:54:22.104 line:80%
<i>Shouldn't Haran also know</i>
<i>that you're fake?</i>

00:54:22.938 --> 00:54:24.982 line:80%
[panting]

00:54:27.609 --> 00:54:28.902 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I told him…</i>

00:54:29.486 --> 00:54:30.738 line:80%
<i>I told Hyeokchan everything.</i>

00:54:31.572 --> 00:54:32.573 line:80%
<i>But…</i>

00:54:33.907 --> 00:54:35.868 line:80%
<i>what happened after that?</i>

00:54:40.664 --> 00:54:42.666 line:80%
[continues panting]

00:54:50.924 --> 00:54:52.676 line:80%
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

00:54:53.552 --> 00:54:54.845 line:80%
It's all my fault.

00:54:55.846 --> 00:54:56.889 line:80%
"Fault…"

00:55:03.979 --> 00:55:05.856 line:80%
-[Raemee] Nineteen.
-Nineteen.

00:55:06.440 --> 00:55:09.151 line:80%
-[Raemee] Thirty-one point five.
-Thirty-one point five.

00:55:09.234 --> 00:55:11.362 line:80%
Everyone, let's keep our spirits up.

00:55:11.445 --> 00:55:13.238 line:80%
When Ms. Kim comes back,

00:55:13.322 --> 00:55:16.283 line:80%
we should show her how much we did
to put her mind at ease.

00:55:16.367 --> 00:55:18.410 line:80%
So how about a quick cheer?

00:55:18.494 --> 00:55:20.245 line:80%
No, forget it.

00:55:21.497 --> 00:55:23.499 line:80%
One, two, three.

00:55:23.582 --> 00:55:24.833 line:80%
[all] Let's do this!

00:55:25.876 --> 00:55:27.044 line:80%
[Chan] Let's do this!

00:55:27.127 --> 00:55:28.295 line:80%
Whatever it is.

00:55:28.379 --> 00:55:29.380 line:80%
-Hey.
-It's Chan.

00:55:29.463 --> 00:55:31.423 line:80%
[Raemee] What's the occasion?
There's no meeting today.

00:55:31.507 --> 00:55:33.717 line:80%
We got the additional script,
so I dropped by.

00:55:33.801 --> 00:55:37.137 line:80%
[smacks lips] And since SHIM is closed,
I made these myself.

00:55:37.221 --> 00:55:38.263 line:80%
I can't guarantee the taste.

00:55:38.347 --> 00:55:39.682 line:80%
-Thank you.
-[Seunggyu] Thank you.

00:55:39.765 --> 00:55:43.435 line:80%
But Ms. Song isn't here right now.

00:55:43.519 --> 00:55:44.645 line:80%
Really?

00:55:44.728 --> 00:55:47.231 line:80%
-Where did she go?
-She took the afternoon off.

00:55:47.314 --> 00:55:51.026 line:80%
Even if Ms. Kim told her not to come,
I guess she's pretty worried.

00:55:51.110 --> 00:55:52.444 line:80%
Did she go to the hospital?

00:55:52.528 --> 00:55:54.905 line:80%
No, she said she had to drop by somewhere.

00:55:54.989 --> 00:55:57.574 line:80%
She had to return something to someone.

00:55:57.658 --> 00:55:58.659 line:80%
Oh…

00:55:59.410 --> 00:56:00.786 line:80%
[Sujin] <i>And my bracelet…</i>

00:56:00.869 --> 00:56:02.746 line:80%
I'm glad you'll give it back to me.

00:56:02.830 --> 00:56:04.415 line:80%
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:56:04.498 --> 00:56:06.125 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:56:06.875 --> 00:56:11.338 line:20%
[navigator] <i>Sunyul National</i>
<i>University Hospital is 1.5 km ahead.</i>

00:56:15.509 --> 00:56:18.095 line:80%
[Sujin] <i>Does she know who you are?</i>

00:56:21.015 --> 00:56:22.182 line:80%
<i>If you provoke me,</i>

00:56:23.392 --> 00:56:27.104 line:80%
<i>even I don't know</i>
<i>what I'll end up telling her.</i>

00:56:28.397 --> 00:56:30.983 line:80%
[♪ music swells]

00:56:31.066 --> 00:56:32.818 line:80%
[panting]

00:56:35.529 --> 00:56:37.531 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:56:44.663 --> 00:56:48.083 line:80%
Ah. The last patient's tone
seemed worse than the tremor.

00:56:48.167 --> 00:56:50.252 line:80%
-Let's reduce the dose.
-[doctor] Okay, I'll check.

00:56:52.671 --> 00:56:54.048 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:56:54.715 --> 00:56:56.091 line:80%
[Chan panting]

00:57:01.972 --> 00:57:02.973 line:80%
[sighs]

00:57:07.353 --> 00:57:09.521 line:80%
-Oh. Haran.
-[Haran] You're here.

00:57:09.605 --> 00:57:12.775 line:80%
Mr. Seonu's upstairs, right?
I have to give him something.

00:57:12.858 --> 00:57:14.526 line:80%
He just left when I came here.

00:57:15.110 --> 00:57:16.487 line:80%
He said he had to go somewhere.

00:57:16.570 --> 00:57:17.571 line:80%
Oh…

00:57:18.405 --> 00:57:21.033 line:80%
Then can I just leave this in his room?

00:57:21.116 --> 00:57:22.618 line:80%
[Manjae] Sure, that's fine.

00:57:22.701 --> 00:57:25.954 line:80%
I'm heading back to the hospital.
I just came to get my stuff.

00:57:26.038 --> 00:57:28.999 line:80%
Then I'll give you a ride.
I'm heading there, too.

00:57:29.083 --> 00:57:30.834 line:80%
No, it's fine. I called a cab.

00:57:30.918 --> 00:57:34.129 line:80%
I made a lot of coffee
to share with the doctors.

00:57:34.213 --> 00:57:36.674 line:80%
I'll leave one for you.

00:57:36.757 --> 00:57:39.760 line:80%
Take your time drinking this
and meet Chan first.

00:57:39.843 --> 00:57:41.345 line:80%
-Okay.
-[Manjae] He'll be back soon.

00:57:43.097 --> 00:57:44.098 line:80%
Mr. Park.

00:57:44.807 --> 00:57:45.808 line:80%
Yes?

00:57:45.891 --> 00:57:48.394 line:80%
Thank you for taking care of my grandma.

00:57:49.645 --> 00:57:51.480 line:80%
[chuckling] Gosh.

00:57:52.231 --> 00:57:53.857 line:80%
There's no need to thank me.

00:57:53.941 --> 00:57:55.943 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:58:00.614 --> 00:58:03.367 line:80%
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
SORRY FOR THE INCONVENIENCE

00:58:09.790 --> 00:58:11.875 line:80%
Pardon me.

00:58:16.296 --> 00:58:19.466 line:80%
[cellphone vibrating]

00:58:19.550 --> 00:58:21.468 line:80%
SEONU CHAN

00:58:22.803 --> 00:58:23.804 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:58:24.555 --> 00:58:26.473 line:80%
[cellphone vibrating]

00:58:31.603 --> 00:58:32.730 line:80%
Hey, roomie.

00:58:33.814 --> 00:58:34.940 line:80%
Yes, she's here.

00:58:35.024 --> 00:58:37.192 line:80%
She brought something for you,
so she went upstairs.

00:58:37.901 --> 00:58:39.528 line:80%
Hang on.

00:58:39.611 --> 00:58:40.863 line:80%
No, it's okay.

00:58:40.946 --> 00:58:42.573 line:80%
I'll be there in a few minutes.

00:58:42.656 --> 00:58:43.866 line:80%
-Really?
-[cellphone chimes]

00:58:43.949 --> 00:58:46.076 line:80%
Huh? My cab's here.

00:58:46.577 --> 00:58:48.203 line:80%
I'm going to the hospital,

00:58:48.704 --> 00:58:50.914 line:80%
so take care of Genius for me.

00:58:53.709 --> 00:58:55.586 line:80%
Is there a Post-it? Oh?

00:58:58.213 --> 00:58:59.214 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:59:14.480 --> 00:59:16.482 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:59:37.586 --> 00:59:38.587 line:80%
Is she upstairs?

00:59:39.546 --> 00:59:40.714 line:80%
Are you here?

00:59:42.341 --> 00:59:43.425 line:80%
Huh?

00:59:47.388 --> 00:59:48.555 line:80%
Hmm?

00:59:51.558 --> 00:59:52.893 line:80%
THANKS FOR THE

00:59:55.562 --> 00:59:56.981 line:80%
[inhales sharply, mumbles]

01:00:00.109 --> 01:00:02.319 line:80%
-[line connects, rings]
-[inhales sharply]

01:00:06.198 --> 01:00:08.200 line:80%
[line continues ringing]

01:00:11.078 --> 01:00:12.871 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:00:25.009 --> 01:00:27.261 line:80%
[thud echoes]

01:00:27.344 --> 01:00:29.680 line:80%
KANG HYEOKCHAN, GLASS TUBE, BLOOD
THAT SOUND AGAIN

01:00:39.481 --> 01:00:42.318 line:20%
KANG HYEOKCHAN HOSPITALIZED, WOMAN
THAT SOUND WAS HER BRACELET

01:00:44.153 --> 01:00:46.322 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I'll tell her everything</i>

01:00:46.405 --> 01:00:47.865 line:80%
<i>and apologize to her.</i>

01:00:48.866 --> 01:00:50.242 line:80%
<i>I want to tell her everything</i>

01:00:50.326 --> 01:00:53.203 line:80%
<i>and love her as my true self…</i>

01:00:54.788 --> 01:00:55.789 line:80%
<i>from now on.</i>

01:00:56.665 --> 01:00:57.708 line:80%
<i>Before it's too late.</i>

01:01:01.253 --> 01:01:02.588 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

01:01:03.172 --> 01:01:05.174 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

01:01:16.977 --> 01:01:18.312 line:80%
Chan.

01:01:18.395 --> 01:01:19.772 line:80%
Why did you come back?

01:01:19.855 --> 01:01:21.148 line:80%
Well…

01:01:21.231 --> 01:01:23.776 line:80%
Did Ms. Song come here?

01:01:23.859 --> 01:01:25.235 line:80%
Hey, what's gotten into you?

01:01:25.319 --> 01:01:27.946 line:80%
-We told you she's going to the hospital.
-Ah…

01:01:30.199 --> 01:01:31.200 line:80%
All right.

01:01:33.994 --> 01:01:38.207 line:80%
Mr. Park, is Ms. Song
at the hospital right now?

01:01:38.290 --> 01:01:40.084 line:80%
No, she's not here.

01:01:40.167 --> 01:01:42.878 line:80%
Did you not see her?

01:01:42.961 --> 01:01:44.004 line:80%
Oh…

01:01:45.005 --> 01:01:46.382 line:80%
It's nothing. Never mind.

01:01:59.687 --> 01:02:02.064 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[Chan pants]

01:02:02.731 --> 01:02:04.608 line:80%
[♪ somber music playing]

01:02:04.692 --> 01:02:06.819 line:80%
RAN

01:02:13.033 --> 01:02:14.493 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Are you home?</i>

01:02:14.576 --> 01:02:16.036 line:80%
<i>If you're home, come out.</i>

01:02:16.120 --> 01:02:18.163 line:80%
<i>Let's meet. Let's meet up and talk.</i>

01:02:18.247 --> 01:02:19.665 line:80%
<i>I'll explain everything.</i>

01:02:38.684 --> 01:02:40.686 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

01:02:58.537 --> 01:03:00.122 line:80%
-Hey…
-[Haran] Don't come any closer.

01:03:07.087 --> 01:03:09.256 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:03:09.340 --> 01:03:10.883 line:80%
Boston Institute of Technology.

01:03:12.426 --> 01:03:14.136 line:80%
Kang Hyeokchan's roommate.

01:03:15.596 --> 01:03:16.972 line:80%
Have you really known me

01:03:18.098 --> 01:03:19.808 line:80%
for seven years?

01:03:25.981 --> 01:03:27.650 line:80%
-Song Haran.
-Don't say my name.

01:03:29.276 --> 01:03:30.778 line:80%
[breath trembling]

01:03:30.861 --> 01:03:32.112 line:80%
Did you have fun

01:03:33.405 --> 01:03:35.032 line:80%
pretending to be Kang Hyeokchan?

01:03:37.618 --> 01:03:38.619 line:80%
[breath trembling]

01:03:38.702 --> 01:03:40.704 line:80%
[♪ emotional song playing]

01:03:46.543 --> 01:03:48.504 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:12.611 --> 01:04:15.614 line:20%
[Chan] <i>She found out about everything.</i>

01:04:15.698 --> 01:04:17.366 line:20%
<i>I didn't have the chance to explain.</i>

01:04:17.449 --> 01:04:19.326 line:20%
[Haran] <i>If those two facts don't change,</i>

01:04:20.035 --> 01:04:21.120 line:20%
<i>I won't change, either.</i>

01:04:21.996 --> 01:04:23.622 line:20%
<i>Don't ever show up in front of me again.</i>

01:04:23.706 --> 01:04:26.959 line:20%
[Chan] <i>You don't have to look at me</i>
<i>or listen to me. So please,</i>

01:04:27.710 --> 01:04:29.253 line:20%
<i>just look at this.</i>

01:04:29.336 --> 01:04:31.755 line:20%
[Hayeong] <i>Haran, you're burning up.</i>

01:04:31.839 --> 01:04:34.466 line:20%
[Nana] <i>You did a great job so far</i>
<i>working by my side.</i>

01:04:34.550 --> 01:04:36.468 line:20%
[Hayeong] <i>Haran's gone.</i>

01:04:36.552 --> 01:04:38.971 line:20%
<i>You're the only one I could ask</i>
<i>where she could be.</i>

01:04:39.054 --> 01:04:41.181 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I have to go find her.</i>

01:04:41.265 --> 01:04:43.267 line:80%
<i>It has to be me.</i>

01:04:45.311 --> 01:04:47.313 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

01:04:47.396 --> 01:04:49.398 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

01:04:55.279 --> 01:04:56.280 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:56.363 --> 01:04:57.364 line:80%
Translated by Juyoung Park